@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "User Guide";
    Layout = "_ContentLayout";
}

<div class="container py-5">
    <h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <p>Welcome to MapLab! This guide will help you get started and make the most of the platform’s features for creating, editing, and sharing interactive maps.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-header">1. Getting Started</h2>
        <p>When you first arrive at MapLab, the <strong>Home Page</strong> is your gateway to all main functions:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Hero Section:</strong> Here you will see the main title <em>"Design Interactive Maps with Ease"</em> and a short description about the platform’s purpose.</li>
            <li><strong>Start Mapping Button:</strong> Click this to jump straight into your map collection if logged in, or be prompted to sign in.</li>
            <li><strong>Watch Demo:</strong> View a quick video demo to familiarize yourself with how the platform works.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-header">2. Exploring Key Features</h2>
        <p>The platform offers three main functionalities you should know about:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Create Interactive Maps:</strong> Use powerful tools to build your own maps from scratch or customize templates.</li>
            <li><strong>Find the Perfect Template:</strong> Search and select from a variety of map templates to jumpstart your project.</li>
            <li><strong>Share and Explore:</strong> Publish your maps publicly or keep them private, and browse community-created maps.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Use the "Learn More" buttons available under each feature to dive deeper into how they work.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-header">3. Managing Your Maps</h2>
        <p>Your personal map collection is displayed with attractive thumbnails (coming soon) and includes:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Map title and template preview (clickable to see details)</li>
            <li>Likes and views statistics</li>
            <li>A stylish "+" button in the lower-right corner to create a new map via a modal window</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Each map has a menu in the upper-right corner with options:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Information:</strong> View map details and similar maps</li>
            <li><strong>Share:</strong> Generate links to share your map</li>
            <li>If you are the owner: <strong>Edit</strong> map details (name, visibility) and <strong>Delete</strong> the map</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-header">4. Creating a Map</h2>
        <p>When creating a new map, you’ll go through a simple two-step process:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Select a Template:</strong> Choose from recently used templates, official MapLab templates, or community recommendations. You can search to find the best fit.</li>
            <li><strong>Name and Set Visibility:</strong> Enter a name for your map and decide if it will be public or private.</li>
        </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-header">5. Editing and Viewing Maps</h2>
        <p>On the map detail page, you have access to three main tools:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>View:</strong> Browse the map without making changes.</li>
            <li><strong>Mark:</strong> Add markers to highlight specific locations.</li>
            <li><strong>Fill:</strong> Color or texture areas of the map to enhance visualization.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The interface includes a legend that tracks your changes and allows easy naming of elements. Undo and redo buttons help manage your edits.</p>
        <p>Save your work with the <strong>Save</strong> button. After editing, you can download your map as an image or share it by generating a link.</p>
        <p>Note: If you are viewing someone else’s map, editing tools will be disabled for security.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-header">6. News and Updates</h2>
        <p>The <strong>News Section</strong> keeps you informed about the latest platform developments:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>View summaries of recent news with titles, dates, and thumbnails.</li>
            <li>Click any news item to read full details.</li>
            <li>Use pagination to browse all news articles.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-header">7. Admin Panel (For Admin Users)</h2>
        <p>If you have admin rights, you can manage the platform via the Admin Panel, which includes:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>User Profiles: Promote or demote users.</li>
            <li>Maps: Delete inappropriate or obsolete maps.</li>
            <li>Map Templates: Add or remove official templates.</li>
            <li>News: Create, edit, or delete news posts.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Advanced filters, sorting, and pagination make managing the platform efficient and straightforward.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-5">
        <h2 class="section-header">8. Taking Action</h2>
        <p>Ready to start your mapping journey?</p>
        <p>
            Use the <strong>Start Mapping</strong> button anywhere on the platform to begin creating your first interactive map. Explore, experiment, and share your creations with the community!
        </p>
        <p>If you want to learn more or revisit this guide, use the <strong>Learn More</strong> buttons or return to this page anytime.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2 class="section-header">9. Need Help?</h2>
        <p>If you encounter any issues or have questions, please contact:</p>
        <p>
            <strong>Simeon Gunev</strong><br />
            @{
                var email = "simganev@gmail.com";
            }
            Email: <a href="mailto:@email">@email</a><br />
            Location: Republic of Bulgaria
        </p>
    </section>
</div>
